      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-293556",
      ":question/problem": "The data below shows the number of $6$-grade math books sold by Bookstore A over a particular six-month period:\n\n$10, 15, 7, 9, 18, 13$\nOver the same period, Bookstore B, selling the same $6$-grade math books, achieved means sales of $10$ books per month.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. Bookstore A achieved mean sales of $10$ books per month.\n2. Bookstore B's monthly mean number of sales is smaller than Bookstore A's.\n3. A comparison of the means suggests that Bookstore A sold fewer books overall than Bookstore B.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
